WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.810
A family brings their
new baby to the gurdwara,

2
00:00:02.860 --> 00:00:05.850
with sweet food and a
cloth for the scripture.

3
00:00:05.900 --> 00:00:07.990
Hymns of joy are sung.

4
00:00:08.040 --> 00:00:11.270
Then the Guru Granth
Sahib is opened at random.

5
00:00:11.320 --> 00:00:12.310
No horoscopes.

6
00:00:12.360 --> 00:00:13.660
No lucky days.

7
00:00:13.710 --> 00:00:16.380
No list of names chosen in advance.

8
00:00:16.430 --> 00:00:21.150
So how can a baby's name come from a
page of scripture opened at random?

9
00:00:21.200 --> 00:00:24.890
In this mission, you'll follow
the naming ceremony step by step,

10
00:00:24.940 --> 00:00:28.060
and read what the Sikh code
of conduct says about it.

11
00:00:28.110 --> 00:00:32.610
Then you'll discover two names
Guru Gobind Singh gave in 1699,

12
00:00:32.660 --> 00:00:35.540
and why Sikhs still
debate how to use them.

13
00:00:35.590 --> 00:00:40.830
Your mission: find out how a page opened
at random can help name a Sikh baby.
